> f1(x: u32 in 0..10000000) = x*x
> g1(x: u32 in 0..10000000) = x*x + (x == 1234567 ? 1 : 0)
> equiv f1 ~ g1
f1 and g1 differ, e.g. x=1234567: 3737254705 vs 3737254706 (found by SAT, checked by evaluation)
> a1(x: u32) = x & 0xffff
> b1(x: u32) = x % 65536
> equiv a1 ~ b1
a1 and b1 are equal on the domain of a1 (proved by SAT: 33 AIG nodes, 0 conflicts)
> p1(x: u32 in 0..20000000) = x where x < 10000000
> q1(x: u32 in 0..20000000) = x + (x == 15000000 ? 1 : 0)
> equiv p1 ~ q1
p1 and q1 are equal on the domain of p1 (proved by SAT: 406 AIG nodes, 62 conflicts)
> p2(x: u32 in 0..20000000) = x where x != 10000000
> q2(x: u32 in 0..20000000) = x + (x == 10000000 ? 7 : 0)
